# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
# Syntax: <from> <to> <status>
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# Canonical feed paths
/feed       /feed.xml          301
/rss        /feed.xml          301
/rss.xml    /feed.xml          301
/atom       /feed.xml          301
/atom.xml   /feed.xml          301

# Canonical sitemap
/sitemap            /sitemap-index.xml  301
/sitemap.xml        /sitemap-index.xml  301

# Common humans-might-type paths
/policy              /editorial-policy   301
/editorial           /editorial-policy   301
/ethics              /editorial-policy   301
/disclosure          /editorial-policy   301
/bio                 /about              301
/owen                /about              301

# Trailing-slash handling: deliberately NOT redirecting directory routes
# like /about/ → /about. Astro emits dist/about/index.html (directory
# style), and Cloudflare Pages normalizes /about ↔ /about/index.html
# automatically. Adding explicit /about/ → /about rules creates a redirect
# loop (Pages internally resolves /about to /about/index.html, then our
# rule fires on the slashed form). Trust Astro's trailingSlash:'never'
# config + Pages' built-in directory handling — they cooperate fine.
